Subject: windows.gaming.input: Windows.Gaming.Input.Preview LegacyGipGameControllerProvider and GameControllerProviderInfo

The IDL is generated from Windows.winmd. Wine has no GIP driver, so there are no GIP devices: FromGameController
and FromGameControllerProvider return no provider, nothing is paired, and nothing is ever sent to a controller.
GetProviderId reports the controller's NonRoamableId. Registering the class makes ApiInformation.IsTypePresent
find it, so Xbox Accessories no longer decides Windows is too old.

